---
source: crates/wn-cli/tests/help.rs
expression: help(path)
---
Install or update the where-next skill for coding agents

Usage: wn skill sync [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --agent <AGENTS>
          Agents to sync (default: those detected in your home directory)
          
          [possible values: claude, codex, cursor, all]

      --path <PATH>
          Repository (or any directory inside it)
          
          [default: .]

      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

      --project
          Install into this repository (`.claude/skills`, `.agents/skills`, `.cursor/skills`) instead of your home directory

      --dry-run
          Show what would change without writing anything

      --model <MODEL>
          Model directory (default: `$WN_MODEL_DIR`, else the best installed model)

      --no-daemon
          Answer in this process instead of the background daemon (also `WN_NO_DAEMON=1`)

      --uninstall
          Remove the skill (and hook) instead

      --any-dir
          Allow a directory outside any git repository, or your home directory or / itself (refused by default: everything under it would be indexed)

  -y, --yes
          Apply without asking

      --color <WHEN>
          Color text output: auto (terminal only; honors NO_COLOR and CLICOLOR_FORCE), always or never
          
          [default: auto]
          [possible values: auto, always, never]

      --from-state
          Re-sync exactly the targets recorded by earlier syncs (used by `wn update`)

      --with-hook
          Also add a Claude Code hook that runs `wn ask --start` on the first prompt of a session in large repositories and adds the hints to the context (off by default)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Shows what it will write and asks first. Only a marked where-next block is ever edited, and
`wn update` re-syncs installed skills.

Examples:
  wn skill sync --dry-run                  show what would change, write nothing
  wn skill sync                            agents detected in your home directory
  wn skill sync --agent claude --yes
  wn skill sync --project                  this repository's .claude/.agents/.cursor skills
  wn skill sync --with-hook                also the Claude Code start-hint hook (large repos only)
  wn skill sync --uninstall
